plete and correct.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added the `GET /api/tags/popular` endpoint. Here are the files I changed:\n\n### Files Modified:\n\n1. **src/tags/tag.repository.ts**\n   - Added `TagWithCount` interface for the response type\n   - Added `listPopular()` method to the repository port interface\n   - Implemented `listPopular()` using Prisma's `_count` aggregation, ordered by article count descending, limited to the specified number\n\n2. **src/tags/tag.service.ts**\n   - Added `listPopular()` method that delegates to the repository\n\n3. **src/tags/tag.routes.ts**\n   - Added new route handler for `GET /tags/popular` that returns the top 10 most-used tags with their counts\n\n4. **tests/tags.integration.test.ts**\n   - Added two new tests to verify the endpoint works correctly\n\n### Additional Fixes (to enable testing):\n\n5. **src/profiles/profile.routes.ts** - Fixed TypeScript type errors\n6. **src/articles/article.routes.ts** - Fixed TypeScript type errors  \n7. **src/comments/comment.routes.ts** - Fixed TypeScript type errors\n\nThe endpoint is now accessible at `/api/tags/popular` and returns JSON in the exact format requested: `{ \"tags\": [ { \"name\": \"<tag>\", \"count\": <number> } ] }`, with the 10 most-used tags sorted by usage count in descending order.","ttft_ms":7004,"type":"result","duration_ms":143092,"uuid":"167c8356-1abc-45bd-8687-aff9f2208117","ttft_stream_ms":4037,"time_to_request_ms":63,"first_content_frame_ms":4038,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
